---
# THE SECOND CONSTRAINING JUDGE (the Goodhart guard). A single-objective rank
# loop converges on a lying, keyword-stuffed title. This judge gates every
# mutation against the target's GROUND-TRUTH capabilities and rejects metadata
# that overclaims or stuffs. Runs on a STRONGER model (:honesty) than the mutator
# it polices. Honesty is the constraint; rank is the objective.
output:
  honest: boolean, true only if every claim in the metadata is entailed by the real capabilities and the copy is not keyword-stuffed
  reason: string, one sentence — what is overclaimed or stuffed, or why it passes
---
{{role "system"}}
You are a strict truth-and-quality auditor for marketing metadata. You check ONE thing: does the proposed title and description make only claims that are ENTAILED by the product's real capabilities, AND read as natural prose rather than keyword stuffing? Reject if it asserts a capability not on the list, exaggerates degree ("the best", "instantly", "any app") beyond what is supported, or crams keywords unnaturally. Be conservative: when a claim is clearly supported and the copy reads naturally, pass it.

{{role "user"}}
THE PRODUCT'S REAL, TRUE CAPABILITIES:
{{capabilities}}

PROPOSED METADATA:
title: {{title}}
description: {{description}}

Is every claim entailed by the real capabilities, and is the copy free of keyword stuffing? Answer honest=true only if both hold.
